{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix \n$F=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(F),$ we reduce the matrix $F$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$rd columns from the original matrix are ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(F)$ is ${{f}_{1},{f}_{2}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-34514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix \n$F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(F).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(F),$ we reduce the matrix $F$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$ is ${{f}_{1},{f}_{2}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix \n$G=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(G).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(G),$ we reduce the matrix $G$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${g}_{1}$ and ${g}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(G)$ is ${{g}_{1},{g}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}].$ \nFind a basis $B$ of  $\\text{Col}(W).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(W),$ we reduce the matrix $W$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is ${{w}_{1},{w}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75073" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix \n$G=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(G).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(G),$ we reduce the matrix $G$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}^{′} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, only the $1$st column is a pivot column, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st column from the original matrix is ${g}_{1}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(G)$ is ${{g}_{1}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-34513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $P$ is given below. Let ${p}_{1}$, ${p}_{2}$, and ${p}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $P.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(P).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${p}_{3}={x}_{1}{p}_{1}+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $P$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$ is ${{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${p}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{3}}={{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{1}}+{{(1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot 1=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["text" "$\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75946" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $T$ is given below. Let ${t}_{1}$, ${t}_{2}$, and ${t}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $T.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${t}_{3}={x}_{1}{t}_{1}+{x}_{2}{t}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $T$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{12}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is ${{t}_{1},{t}_{3}}.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["text" "$\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111508" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $T$ is given below. Let ${t}_{1}$, ${t}_{2}$, and ${t}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $T.$ Determine if $B=\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(T).$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${t}_{3}={x}_{1}{t}_{1}+{x}_{2}{t}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 30\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $T$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is ${{t}_{1},{t}_{2}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${t}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{t}_{3}}={{(2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{t}_{1}}+{{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{t}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 3=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["text" "$\\text{{}{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-111502" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $U$ is given below. Let ${u}_{1}$, ${u}_{2}$, and ${u}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $U.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{u}_{1},{u}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(U).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${u}_{2}={x}_{1}{u}_{1}+{x}_{3}{u}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reduce the matrix $U$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(U)$ is ${{u}_{1},{u}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${u}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{u}_{2}}={{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{u}_{1}}+{{(0)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{u}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=(-2)\\cdot 0=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7caedf66fd15c6d3ca127277becd3f0134e88844518f3813822fa03b768342"} {"question" "q-75083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9c2b63f5d45a60d8ee1e2ed45e3529279858153457a40174d5"} {"question" "q-75083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["text" "$\\text{{}{u}_{1},{u}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(U)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066433/state.json" "file_sha256" "56b80f879c946e9